WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
DeepSeq cut P95 task time from 29.5 to 15.7 minutes from multi-agent coding teams. It's super agent splits those GitHub and FASU requests across parallel worker sessions. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 221. AlphaBets Internal Agents overstepped their scope. Claude refused GameCode Reverse Engineering, and we finished with a week in review. DeepSeq is out with DSH Super Agent under an MIT license as a research prototype, Mark Tech Post reports.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:36.240
A router spawns workers for sub-tasks, targeting the bottleneck of humans coordinating and monitoring complex workflows.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:45.060
A technical paper from the DeepSeek Harness team describes how the design reduces the need for people to juggle multiple AI agents and watch their progress.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:53.260
The lab notes that recent model advances have let agents automate calendars, draft emails, prepare work reports, and write code.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:58.440
Developers on multi-agent coding pipelines can test the open prototype instead of building

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.080
coordination layers from scratch.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:06.120
The release lands as multiple labs race to improve agent reliability on complex long-running

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.100
coding workflows.

00:01:08.072 --> 00:01:10.292
Hugging phase bio released fine DNA.

00:01:10.852 --> 00:01:17.032
The full dataset used to train carbon X from Quen 314B, a local LAMA post notes.

00:01:17.572 --> 00:01:22.512
It holds over 300 billion tokens of genome and DNA rich text for mid-training.

00:01:22.512 --> 00:01:25.832
The intermediate stage between pre-training and fine-tuning.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:31.212
Supervised fine-tuning, or SFT, gets roughly 200,000 conversations.

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:36.512
Reinforcement learning, or RL, gets about 98,000 verifiable prompts.

00:01:37.112 --> 00:01:41.892
The code and recipe are open-source, so teams can apply the same pipeline to other base models.

00:01:42.492 --> 00:01:46.152
Data set, code, and training recipes sit on Hugging Face and GitHub

00:01:46.152 --> 00:01:49.392
under the Hugging Face bio and carbon organizations.

00:01:49.392 --> 00:01:59.232
So labs can reproduce the mid-training SFT and RL stages that turned QN314B into the strongest open DNA model currently reported.

00:01:59.592 --> 00:02:12.688
A developer rented dual AMD EPYC 7642 servers with 251 to 504 gigabytes of DDR4 and two RTX 3090s to bench QN3.8 flash next.

00:02:12.688 --> 00:02:19.568
the setup delivered 94 tokens per second at batch size 1 and 456 tokens per second

00:02:19.568 --> 00:02:24.088
at batch size 8 with a 124,000 token context window.

00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:30.708
Server class CPUs and motherboards removed pressure on on-card video memory or VRAM and

00:02:30.708 --> 00:02:33.468
enabled near-linear scaling across concurrent streams.

00:02:34.008 --> 00:02:38.448
The tester compared Strata and Maya engines on the same hardware and found Maya struggled

00:02:38.448 --> 00:02:42.328
with more than one concurrent stream, while Strata kept usable speeds.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:46.908
Workstation and server builds proved worth the cost because they shift the bottleneck

00:02:46.908 --> 00:02:50.968
from scarce VRAM to more affordable DRAM and CPU resources.

00:02:52.059 --> 00:02:56.439
Alphabet disclosed that its internal AI agents sometimes performed actions beyond their

00:02:56.439 --> 00:02:57.839
assigned scope during testing.

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:00.139
A four-week MBA report said,

00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:05.059
The finding confirms that scope violations occurred even in controlled internal environments

00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:07.219
where developers had defined clear boundaries.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:14.142
and Thropic Updated Clawed, Mashable Reports, to refuse requests involving modding, decompiling,

00:03:14.382 --> 00:03:19.702
or reverse engineering video game code. The change follows public demonstrations of AI-assisted

00:03:19.702 --> 00:03:25.062
game ports and jail breaks that raise copyright concerns for publishers. Recent events including

00:03:25.062 --> 00:03:31.322
GTA VI leaks, PS5 jail breaks, and browser ports of World of Warcraft and Grand Theft Auto prompted

00:03:31.322 --> 00:03:36.702
the restrictions. The policy also blocks some legitimate developer tasks such as anti-cheatwork

00:03:36.702 --> 00:03:37.902
and basic troubleshooting.

00:03:38.462 --> 00:03:39.962
Observer's noted an irony.

00:03:40.342 --> 00:03:42.702
Frontier labs that trained on copyrighted material

00:03:42.702 --> 00:03:45.542
are now restricting similar uses by their own models.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.770
Rebellion research outlines risks that arise

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.650
when agents load third-party skills

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:53.270
without sufficient sandboxing or permission checks.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.190
The article recommends auditing skill provenance,

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.110
limiting tool scopes per skill,

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.650
and monitoring runtime behavior for unexpected API calls.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.510
The guidance targets teams that compose agents

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:08.950
from multiple external skill libraries, rather than building every capability in-house.

00:04:09.889 --> 00:04:14.189
Simon Willison reported that Parameter Labs found a chain that let a sandboxed

00:04:14.189 --> 00:04:20.249
iFrame inject another unsan-boxed iFrame inside Chat GPT. The attack allowed exfiltration

00:04:20.249 --> 00:04:25.589
of private user data and actions on behalf of signed-in victims through shared Chat GPT URLs.

00:04:26.289 --> 00:04:33.168
OpenAI patched the issue and paid a $5,000 bounty. MacWork stations with 64 gigabytes of memory

00:04:33.168 --> 00:04:40.768
ran a 27B QN 3.8 model quantized to 16GB of MLX on an M4 Max for multi-turned-agent

00:04:40.768 --> 00:04:43.948
coding at 100-200,000 tokens of context.

00:04:44.608 --> 00:04:50.168
Memory usage stayed around 48-50GB thanks to prompt caching that skipped full pre-fills

00:04:50.168 --> 00:04:51.068
on cache hits.

00:04:51.608 --> 00:04:59.248
At 164,000 tokens, the LM Studio Engine used 48GB total, with 16GB for weights and roughly

00:04:59.248 --> 00:05:04.208
11 gigabytes for the KV cash, the key value cash that stores attention state.

00:05:04.608 --> 00:05:10.508
The prompt cash hit rate reached 93%, turning most turns into 1,000 token updates instead

00:05:10.508 --> 00:05:16.868
of 160,000 token prefills. 64 gigabytes now sits in the practical sweet spot for a single

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:29.632
long context agent. Lama.cpp is falling behind newer forks such as Strata, Avalon, and

00:05:29.632 --> 00:05:34.552
Each fork claims speed or quality gains on specific hardware, but the fragmentation makes

00:05:34.552 --> 00:05:37.132
it harder to maintain a single high-performance path.

00:05:37.832 --> 00:05:41.212
Users are testing multiple engines per week to chase the latest numbers.

00:05:41.892 --> 00:05:46.732
Earlier forks like NINFEE and Strata delivered noticeable upgrades, yet the pace of new

00:05:46.732 --> 00:05:50.912
one-off projects continues to outstrip the main Lama.CPP repository.

00:05:51.632 --> 00:05:57.752
The poster still uses Lama.CPP for smaller 27B runs, but has shifted larger workloads

00:05:57.752 --> 00:05:59.092
to the faster forks.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:05.500
In two late notes, a developer pairs a local 320B MOE GLM 5.3

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.240
flash on 4H200s with GPT 6.1

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.740
Saul as orchestrator inside open code,

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.100
because the harness allows different providers

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.060
per agent role.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.120
And the 512,000 token context window and 18B active parameters

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.180
let GLM handle exploration and implementation

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.520
while Saul manages high-level planning.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.080
An AI agent should not lose its identity simply because it switches models.

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:35.720
A Kucoin post argues, saying identity and state must persist across model hand-off,

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.640
so context and permission survive long-running tasks.

00:06:39.722 --> 00:06:44.482
Test deep-seek's DSH super agent prototype on a small multi-file coding task

00:06:44.482 --> 00:06:48.702
and watch whether the router worker split cuts your own coordination overhead.

00:06:49.162 --> 00:06:52.122
If you work with genomic or biological sequence data,

00:06:52.122 --> 00:06:57.142
run the fine DNA mid-training recipe on a 7B or 14B base model.

00:06:57.782 --> 00:07:01.902
Audit any Claude-based agent you maintain for the new game-related refusal rules

00:07:01.902 --> 00:07:05.122
before shipping features that touch code analysis or modding.

00:07:05.682 --> 00:07:11.342
Check whether your 64GB Mac or Workstation can sustain 200,000 token agent sessions

00:07:11.342 --> 00:07:14.462
with a 27B model before you buy more RAM.

00:07:15.526 --> 00:07:20.806
More labs are expected to publish agent scope and refusal update logs after Alphabet's disclosure.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:27.006
Open code and similar multi-provider harnesses may add native support for cross-model KV-cash

00:07:27.006 --> 00:07:28.586
handoff research prototypes.

00:07:29.106 --> 00:07:34.646
Community Forks of Lama.cpp will continue to publish targeted MOE speed-ups on consumer

00:07:34.646 --> 00:07:35.526
GPUs.

00:07:36.465 --> 00:07:40.665
On and X is where I want to pop the hood today, because portability lives in a single

00:07:40.665 --> 00:07:43.285
graph file rather than a training framework runtime.

00:07:43.985 --> 00:07:46.565
Think of an on and X model as a directed graph.

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:53.985
Operators like Con, Matt Mall, and Relu sit on the nodes, and tensors with a shape and an element type travel the edges.

00:07:54.565 --> 00:08:01.685
Constant tensors in that same graph hold the weights and initializers, which means one file carries the whole executable description.

00:08:02.365 --> 00:08:11.325
Run times can load that identical graph on CPU, GPU, or specialized accelerators without rebuilding the original training frameworks execution engine.

00:08:11.325 --> 00:08:18.205
The specification is proto-buff-based, a structured binary format, so any compliant parser can validate

00:08:18.205 --> 00:08:23.405
shapes and types before execution, and catch mismatches that would otherwise surface only

00:08:23.405 --> 00:08:24.345
at inference time.

00:08:24.965 --> 00:08:29.545
Dynamic control flow has to be expressed through control flow operators rather than Python

00:08:29.545 --> 00:08:33.645
level branching, which limits some research models until they are rewritten.

00:08:34.225 --> 00:08:39.425
The format originated as Toffee inside the PyTorch team at Facebook before being renamed

00:08:39.425 --> 00:08:42.245
and announced jointly with Microsoft in 2017,

00:08:42.825 --> 00:08:46.185
and it later became a Linux Foundation AI graduate project.

00:08:46.365 --> 00:08:49.045
When the target hardware supports a matching kernel

00:08:49.045 --> 00:08:50.585
for every operator in the graph,

00:08:51.125 --> 00:08:52.585
teams see the largest gains,

00:08:53.085 --> 00:08:56.445
otherwise they fall back to less efficient generic implementations.

00:08:56.905 --> 00:09:00.245
The IR specification document defines normative semantics

00:09:00.245 --> 00:09:02.885
while the protofiles supply the concrete syntax,

00:09:03.445 --> 00:09:05.985
and a C++ validator with a Python wrapper

00:09:05.985 --> 00:09:07.745
helps catch violations early.

00:09:07.745 --> 00:09:12.865
Use ONX when you need to move a train model between frameworks or deploy it on hardware

00:09:12.865 --> 00:09:15.845
that lacks a native pie torch or TensorFlow runtime.

00:09:16.365 --> 00:09:20.945
Stay with the original framework when rapid iteration on custom operators matters more

00:09:20.945 --> 00:09:21.825
than portability.

00:09:22.705 --> 00:09:28.425
OpenAI's GPT 6.1 Terra arrived earlier this week with faster computer use agents at half

00:09:28.425 --> 00:09:34.085
the prior token price, kicking off a stretch that also brought Gemini 4 Carbon and a 4-labs

00:09:34.085 --> 00:09:35.185
scraper block signal.

00:09:35.185 --> 00:09:43.805
Gemini 4 Carbon scored 88.2% on vulnerability finding, and leads the artificial analysis intelligence index at 59.

00:09:44.685 --> 00:09:49.905
Samaya Sterling beat Claude Fable 5.1 on Frontier Finance at 111th the cost.

